# Bytes are the identity in this repository -- digests are taken over file
# contents -- so Git must never rewrite line endings, in either direction, on
# any platform. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, and
# without this line a clone there converts all 1,557 LF text files to CRLF: every
# fixture read from the working tree then hashes differently than it does on
# Linux or macOS, and the failures surface far from their cause.
#
# `-text` (never convert) rather than `text=auto eol=lf` (normalize on checkin)
# on purpose. text=auto lets Git decide what is text and rewrite it while
# committing, which is the same class of silent byte mangling -- it would corrupt
# a fixture whose whole point was to carry CRLF. No tracked file contains CR
# today, so this is protective, not a migration. It does not affect diffs: the
# `text` attribute governs eol conversion only, `diff` is a separate attribute.
* -text

# PDF fixtures contain fixed-width cross-reference records, including spaces.
# Preserve their bytes and avoid text diffs or text merges of binary documents.
crates/kio-eval/acceptance-fixtures/**/*.pdf binary

# Security audit exports preserve source bytes for receipt and checksum bindings.
security/audits/** -whitespace
